A method for controlling electric power, including:

- measuring current;
- calculating a command value;
- carrying out an operation;
- deciding whether an operation interval during which the operation is carried out should be changed to exceed one carrier-wave cycle;
- after changing the operation interval, suppressing switching of the switching elements during an initial half-cycle of the carrier wave, beginning at the start of the changed operation interval, in which the carrier wave varies monotonically;
- during an intermediate interval located between the initial half-cycle and a final half-cycle of the carrier wave within the changed operation interval, modifying the carrier-wave slope, comparing the magnitude of the carrier wave with that of a duty-command value, and switching the switching elements based on the comparison result; and
- suppressing switching of the switching elements during the final half-cycle of the carrier wave.

